Z||000000||Jim Keyton||01-27-2001||10:08 AM||||Has anyone installed the Ravin' muffler from Midas? Are they only available at Midas? The local Midas shops want $189.00 for the series 55 single inlet dual outlet. Seems high for a muffler.||||reg||1
Z||000001||RNGCRSH||01-27-2001||03:05 PM||||Of course Midas wants alot, everything they touch turns to gold.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Personaly I wouldn't bring my car to midas for anything. They only exist because of stupid/ignorant pepole who don't care or don't know what they are paying for.<P>I brought my company car to Midas once for a small brake problem. They wanted over $2000 dollars to fix. they gave me a list a mile long of parts needed (The brakes had less than 500 miles on them).It was too much so I brought it to the dealer for an estimate. It was $250 to repair parts and labor for a new proportioning valve and brake line broken removing valve. (I was out of town when this happened so I could not bring it to my normal mechanic).<P>I know this refers to brakes not thier mufflers but they use the same business tactics for all of thier sales. <P>Midas will sell you more than what you need at a higher price with inflated labor cost.<P>Thats my opinion!<p>[This message has been edited by RNGCRSH (edited 01-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shiner||01-27-2001||03:16 PM||||Hmm, that sure sounds like a solid endorsement!  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||01-27-2001||03:18 PM||||I agree about never taking anything to Midas. I had a lifetime muffler put on Mom's Cavalier and I took it back when the muffler rusted out. I had my original ticket but they would not make the repairs because they said the cat. converter and y-pipe were rotted out and could not fix just the muffler. There was nothing wrong with the converter- it was less than 1 year old and the y-pipe was a aftermarket stainless one. They just refused to stand behind their products.||||reg||1
